title: Key state reconciliation and reporting in rc-client and ah-client
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    Closes #12443.

    Asset Hub moves the session-key deposit optimistically and never learns what the relay chain did with
    the keys. `rc_client::purge_keys` released the `KeyDeposit` **before** RC confirmed the purge, and
    `ah_client::{set_keys,purge_keys}_from_ah` swallowed the `DispatchError` and returned `Ok(())`. If RC
    kept the keys, that is a validator with live session keys and no deposit backing them.

    The reachable failure is `DuplicatedKey` on set: the keys are already owned by another stash. AH
    cannot pre-check it, because the key-owner registry lives on RC. Today that leaves the deposit held
    against keys that were never registered.

    RC now reports its resulting key state after every key operation, and AH reconciles the hold against
    it. No new storage items, and no XCM types added to `rc-client`.

    # Integration

    Four things downstream relay-chain runtimes must do, plus one operational constraint.

    **1. `SendToAssetHub` gains a method.** Every implementation must add it:

    ```diff
    +    fn relay_keys_state(stash: Self::AccountId, has_keys: bool) -> Result<(), ()> {
    +        rc_client::XCMSender::<
    +            xcm_config::XcmRouter,
    +            AssetHubLocation,
    +            (AccountId, bool),
    +            KeysStateToXcm,
    +        >::send((stash, has_keys))
    +    }
    ```

    **2. A new call variant and converter**, mirroring the existing `SessionReportToXcm`.

    ```diff
    +    #[codec(index = 12)]
    +    RelayKeysState { stash: AccountId, has_keys: bool },
    ```

    ```rust
    pub struct KeysStateToXcm;
    impl Convert<(AccountId, bool), Xcm<()>> for KeysStateToXcm {
        fn convert((stash, has_keys): (AccountId, bool)) -> Xcm<()> {
            Xcm(vec![
                Instruction::UnpaidExecution {
                    weight_limit: WeightLimit::Unlimited,
                    check_origin: None,
                },
                Instruction::Transact {
                    origin_kind: OriginKind::Superuser,
                    fallback_max_weight: None,
                    call: AssetHubRuntimePallets::RcClient(RcClientCalls::RelayKeysState {
                        stash,
                        has_keys,
                    })
                    .encode()
                    .into(),
                },
            ])
        }
    }
    ```

    **3. `ah_client::Config::SessionInterface` gains a bound.**
    ```diff
         type SessionInterface: SessionInterface<
                 ValidatorId = Self::AccountId,
                 AccountId = Self::AccountId,
    -        >;
    +        > + ValidatorRegistration<Self::AccountId>;
    ```

    **4. Behaviour change on AH.** `rc_client::purge_keys` no longer releases the deposit
    synchronously. It is released when RC reports back. Anything asserting an immediate release will need
    updating.

    **5. Deployment order: RC before AH.**

    - *RC first is safe.* RC sends a call index AH does not have yet, the `Transact` fails to decode, the
      message is dropped.
    - *AH first is not.* AH stops releasing on purge while no report exists, so anyone who purges and
      walks away has a permanently stuck deposit.

    No storage migrations.

    # Review Notes

    ## Design Consideration

    ```rust
    // ah-client, after every set/purge attempt
    T::SendToAssetHub::relay_keys_state(stash, T::SessionInterface::is_registered(&stash));

    // rc-client, gated by RelayChainOrigin
    has_keys  => hold == KeyDeposit   // `set_on_hold` is exact, so it also fixes a stale hold
    !has_keys => release_all
    ```
    `purge_keys` only sends; `set_keys` still holds at call time, so the funds cannot be spent in flight.

    To keep things not too convoluted: This is a **state assertion, not an ack**. A ack would've needed nonces, timeouts and other wiring. This solutions is minimal, reuses existing state and messes with no public API.

    ## Open question for reviewers

    - Key ops were not gated on OperatingMode(on either clients), unlike other outgoing messages, so I kept it that way. I would introduce those here though.

    ## Testing

    87 integration tests and 6 `ah-client` unit tests pass.

    - `set_keys_rejected_by_rc_refunds_deposit`: the critical case. A stash sets keys another account
      already owns on RC. RC rejects with `DuplicatedKey`. AH refunds. Asserts the specific RC error, so it
      cannot pass via an unrelated failure.
    - `purge_releases_deposit_only_once_rc_reports`: with the report's delivery failed, RC has purged but
      AH still holds. a later report releases it.
    - `last_report_wins`: report orderings including `[false, true]`, the purge-and-set-in-flight case,
      plus correction of a hold left stale by a `KeyDeposit` change.
    - `keys_without_a_coverable_deposit_are_reported`: covers the `KeyDepositUnavailable` branch.
    - `key_ops_report_resulting_state_to_ah`: all four paths report what `is_registered` says,
      including a failed set while keys are already registered reporting `true`.
    - `set_and_purge_keys_e2e` gained deposit assertions on both legs.

    Two pre-existing tests changed assertions: `purge_keys_success` and
    `set_keys_deposit_lifecycle` both encoded the eager release. They run in `local_queue()` mode, where
    the message is buffered and no report arrives, so the deposit correctly stays held.

    ## TODOs

    - prdoc.
    - `relay_keys_state` uses a hand written weight, consistent with the other RC->AH calls
      in this pallet. Benchmark this?
    - `RemoteKeysExecutionWeight` in `asset-hub-westend/src/staking.rs` might need a bump for the extra
      RC-side send.

    # Checklist

    * [x] My PR includes a detailed description as outlined in the "Description" and its two subsections above.
    * [ ] My PR follows the [[labeling requirements](https://github.com/paritytech/polkadot-sdk/blob/master/docs/contributor/CONTRIBUTING.md#Process)](https://github.com/paritytech/polkadot-sdk/blob/master/docs/contributor/CONTRIBUTING.md#Process) of this project (at minimum one label for `T` required)
    * [x] I have made corresponding changes to the documentation (if applicable)
    * [x] I have added tests that prove my fix is effective or that my feature works (if applicable)
crates:
- name: pallet-staking-async-rc-client
  bump: major
- name: westend-runtime
  bump: major
- name: pallet-staking-async-ah-client
  bump: major
